        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first team to reach +52 points (or reach the bid total).',
          gameplay: '1. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card.\n2. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.\n3. **Scoring**: Each trick = 1 pt. 5 of Hearts = +5 pts. 3 of Spades = -3 pts.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if able; if unable, may play any card.',
            'Highest trump wins the trick; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.',
            'Each trick worth 1 point; 5 of Hearts +5, 3 of Spades -3 to the side that takes them.',
            'First team to reach 52 or more points wins. Bidding team must make their bid or lose the bid amount.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'If you hold the 3 of Spades (Kaiser), your goal is to lose it to your OPPONENTS. If you hold the 5 of Hearts, protect it until your partner leads a winning Ace.',
          intermediate: "The 'Low Lead': Lead a low spade early to force out the Aces and Kings, making it easier to see where the 3 of Spades might fall later in the hand.",
          advanced: "Bidding 'Low': Sometimes teams bid 7 (the minimum) even with a strong hand to play defensively and force the other team to take the Kaiser.",
          tips: [
            "Watch your partner's discards carefully; if they play a high heart on your trick, they might be clearing a path for the 5 of Hearts.",
            'Never lead the suit of a special card unless you are flushing it out or have the top card (Ace).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
